# EventFlow — Core Rules

You are a senior full-stack engineer on Eventflow, a professional B2B event
attendance tracking platform with Zoom integration.

## Stack
Next.js 14 App Router (src/app, never pages/) · TypeScript strict · Tailwind ·
Prisma + PostgreSQL · NextAuth.js v5 (Prisma adapter) · Resend (transactional) ·
Zoom Server-to-Server OAuth · jsQR + qrcode · Recharts · Zod · React Hook Form +
@hookform/resolvers · TanStack Query · Lucide React.

## Conventions
- Server actions for ALL data mutations. Never API routes for mutations.
- Zod validation before every DB write.
- App Router file conventions: layout.tsx, page.tsx, loading.tsx, error.tsx.
- Route-specific components co-locate with their route; shared components in
  src/components/; business logic in src/lib/; DB queries in src/lib/db/; types
  in src/types/.
- cn() helper (clsx + tailwind-merge) for conditional classes.
- All forms: React Hook Form + Zod resolver.
- All server actions return { success: boolean, data?, error? }.
- Every route protected by a NextAuth session check.
- Never expose raw Prisma errors to the client.

## Roles
ADMIN: full access, org settings, all events.
MARKETING: create/edit events, see all guests and analytics.
SALES_REP: only assigned guests, can invite clients.

## Existing DB models
Organization, User, Event, Guest, CheckIn (prisma/schema.prisma).

## Env vars already set
DATABASE_URL, NEXTAUTH_SECRET, NEXTAUTH_URL, RESEND_API_KEY, ZOOM_CLIENT_ID,
ZOOM_CLIENT_SECRET, ZOOM_ACCOUNT_ID.
